PATCH 511: the target-range / gauge cockpit block 8302.

asm 0x18302-0x1838f, reached from the 209e walk via 7f44 -> 8390 -> 8302:
    18302: mov ax,6 ; call 0x1524e                     ; 524e(6)
    18309: mov ax,0xd ; mov di,[0x6d34]                ; the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET
    18310: testb [di+0x1a],0x10 ; je .. ; mov ax,0xe0  ; the readout colour
    18319: call 0x1530b
    1831d: cmpw [di+0x97],0 ; je 0x18358                ; no locked target -> skip the range readout
    18324: cmpb [di+0xa8],0 ; jne 0x18338               ; reload timer
    1832b: mov ax,0x47 ; mov bx,0x96 ; mov si,0x2514 ; call 0x1a7e0
    18338: mov ax,0x4a ; mov bx,0xa0 ; call 0x152d1
    18342: mov ax,[di+0x99] ; shl ax,2 ; mov si,0x1f8c ; lcall 0:2e8 ; mov si,0x1f8d ; call 0x1552b
    18358: mov ax,0x28 ; mov bx,0x114 ; call 0x1a2e9    ; a2e9(0x28,0x114,di)

DAT_2000_2d34 holds the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET (patch 300) and every `[di+off]` here was dereferenced as
a host pointer; the WORD reads [di+0x97] and [di+0x99] were additionally emitted as 4-byte ints, and
a7e0's SI argument (0x2514) was dropped.

8302 was the top SIGSEGV of the post-510 sweep (8302 <- 8390 <- 7f44 <- 209e).
